         <description><![CDATA[<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/979387a3-79f1-47a7-b640-2d1511ceea90,1794006730082/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C2048%2C1152%29%3B' alt='An aerial image shows a large fir tree on a residential street.' width='620' height='349' title='The white fir at 65 Fortieth St. was described by neighbours as a staple of the community.'/><p>A Toronto developer is facing new accusations of illegal tree removal at a residential property in Etobicoke. Four trees were recently cut down without permits at a property connected to Modcity. The company denies any wrongdoing.</p>]]></description>
